-- title:
--   Maximal unramified extensions under constant field extension (EtPi1Geo library, file 02)
-- statement:
--   Library for comparing fundamental groups of curves over a finite field and over its algebraic closure. For a domain $A$ with fraction field $K$, $K_U \subset \overline{K}$ is the maximal extension of $K$ unramified over $A$ and $\pi_1 = \mathrm{Gal}(K_U/K)$ (Krull topology); for $K$ of characteristic $p$ and $q$ a power of $p$, $\pi_1^{\mathrm{geo}} \le \pi_1$ is the subgroup fixing every constant ($x^{q^n} = x$). Built on the flat curve library (`Def_RPLib_F2_032`). Contents: for $FK$ generated over $F$ by constants, an element of $\overline{F}$ that lies in a finite Galois extension unramified over $A$ after adjoining constants lies in $K_U(A, F)$; hence the maximal unramified extension of $FK$ over the integral closure of $A$ is the image of $K_U(A, F)$.
-- source:
--   A. Grothendieck, Revêtements étales et groupe fondamental (SGA 1), Lecture Notes in Math. 224, Springer (1971), Exposés V and IX; J. S. Milne, Étale Cohomology, Princeton University Press (1980), Chapter I; J.-P. Serre, Local Fields, GTM 67, Springer (1979), Chapter I

